  "articleBody": "Getting that perfectly smooth, seamless look for your room addition's drywall really boils down to avoiding some common pitfalls. One frequent mistake is rushing the drywall installation before the rough-ins (electrical, plumbing, HVAC) are fully complete and inspected. Once that drywall goes up, those systems are hidden, and you absolutely need them checked out first. Another big issue is overlooking uneven framing. If your framing isn't perfectly plumb and level, those imperfections will show right through the drywall, no matter how skilled the installer. You’ll end up with wavy walls or ceilings. Finally, many folks underestimate how much the chosen finish level impacts labor time and cost. A level 5 smooth finish, for example, requires significantly more work and skill than a basic texture. Trying to cut corners here often leads to a disappointing final result. To avoid these headaches, make sure all preceding trades are done and inspected. Also, pay close attention during the framing stage to ensure everything is straight and true. If you’re aiming for a high-quality, perfectly smooth finish, or if there are specific requirements like moisture-resistant drywall, a skilled drywall and finish contractor can make all the difference, ensuring a professional, long-lasting result.",
